This is the published crate, unpacked as-is (Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock,
Cargo.toml.orig, README.md, build.rs, locales/, src/, tests/). The crate
version and public API are unchanged; it replaces the registry copy through
[patch.crates-io] in native/Cargo.toml.

Local changes (V2-U57), both marked "ZeeTerm local change" in the source and
shown in full by LOCAL-CHANGES.patch:
- src/styled.rs: new crate-private focus_outline(), a 2px outline in the ring
  colour separated from the element by a clear 2px gap, plus two constants.
- src/button/button.rs: when a button has keyboard focus and Theme::focus_ring
  is off, it draws that outline instead of the 1px focus line that
  focus_style() falls back to. With Theme::focus_ring on, nothing changes.

Why it is not done in the application: Theme::focus_ring is one global switch
read by every control. The application keeps it off so text inputs show a
single accent border instead of border plus halo (V2-U17); turning it on again
would bring the double frame back, and per-button styling is not exposed by
Button (the focus outline is drawn inside Button::render, and the application
cannot reach the buttons that the library builds itself).

To verify the original bytes and the exact change, from native/vendor:
  unpack the .crate (a gzip tar) into an empty directory, check its SHA-256 as
  above, then `diff -ru <unpacked>/gpui-component-0.8.1 gpui-component-0.8.1`
  must show only LOCAL-CHANGES.patch, src/styled.rs and src/button/button.rs,
  and the last two must match LOCAL-CHANGES.patch.
When gpui-kit / gpui-component is upgraded, re-evaluate this change and drop
the vendor directory if upstream gives buttons a visible focus outline.
